---
const sides = [
  {
    label: 'From source code',
    title: 'JetBrains plugin',
    text: 'Generates the AsyncAPI document from Spring Messaging code and flags listener mistakes in the editor. When the code changes, you review the difference.',
    href: '/jetbrains-plugin/',
    cta: 'See the plugin',
  },
  {
    label: 'The contract',
    title: 'One AsyncAPI document',
    text: 'The single place that says what your system does, validated against the AsyncAPI JSON Schemas by editors, CI pipelines and AI agents.',
    href: '/schemas/registry.html',
    cta: 'Use the schema registry',
  },
  {
    label: 'From brokers and queues',
    title: 'Kurkik',
    text: 'Reads a live Kafka, Pulsar, SNS or SQS system, shows where it differs from the document, and applies fixes only as a plan you approve.',
    href: 'https://kurkik.pavelon.dev',
    cta: 'Read about Kurkik',
  },
]
---

<section class="section" id="drift">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Self-maintaining AsyncAPI</span>
      <h2>Drift, caught from both sides</h2>
      <p>
        An AsyncAPI document is a promise. Code changes, topics get added, queues get reconfigured, and the promise quietly stops being
        true. These tools compare the declaration with what actually runs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="flow">
      {
        sides.map((s, i) => (
          <li class:list={['card', { middle: i === 1 }]}>
            <span class="label">{s.label}</span>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
            <a class="more" href={s.href}>
              {s.cta} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .flow {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .flow {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .middle {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    flex: 1;
  }
</style>
